# BusyBox applets for the flasher's init, Lemnos's init scripts (packaging/init, da86d0b3) and Orion's
# (packaging/busybox, 3f60576c). From B9 (b2efaf42), with the four Orion's scripts add, and the network's (flasher-lemnos0).
# Gaia's Buildroot base is allnoconfig, so an applet is on only when this file says so. Each line:
# ash        /bin/sh: the Lemnos scripts are POSIX sh run under ash, and rcS runs them
# init       PID 1 (BR2_INIT_BUSYBOX): /etc/inittab and rcS
# getty      the console getty on ttyGS0 (BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY)
# login      what getty starts for a login (root without a password, the console policy in the OS fragment)
# mount      rcS mounts proc, sys and devtmpfs
# start-stop-daemon  S50lemnosd and S51lemnos-orion start their supervisors with it (the script says so)
# mdev       device nodes at boot (mdev -s) and on hotplug; the Lemnos rules are an mdev.conf fragment
# sleep, kill, cat, date, rm, mkdir, touch, dirname, test ([)  used by the two init scripts
# sync, reboot, poweroff, halt  the shutdown path of init
# chgrp, chmod, chown, su  Orion's S40orion-comm and orion-supervise: the socket's group and mode, node logic as orion
# sha256sum, cut, tr, mv  lemnos0-address (the serial-hash-v1 script) and S39flasher-net
# cp                      S39flasher-net copies the fixed Orion settings
# ip (addr, link)         S39flasher-net gives lemnos0 the board's address and brings it up
# udhcpd                  S39flasher-net's DHCP server, so a stock PC takes an address on the /29 with no configuration
CONFIG_ASH=y
CONFIG_INIT=y
CONFIG_GETTY=y
CONFIG_LOGIN=y
CONFIG_MOUNT=y
CONFIG_UMOUNT=y
CONFIG_START_STOP_DAEMON=y
CONFIG_MDEV=y
CONFIG_FEATURE_MDEV_CONF=y
CONFIG_SLEEP=y
CONFIG_KILL=y
CONFIG_CAT=y
CONFIG_DATE=y
CONFIG_RM=y
CONFIG_MKDIR=y
CONFIG_TOUCH=y
CONFIG_DIRNAME=y
CONFIG_TEST=y
CONFIG_SYNC=y
CONFIG_REBOOT=y
CONFIG_POWEROFF=y
CONFIG_HALT=y
CONFIG_CHGRP=y
CONFIG_CHMOD=y
CONFIG_CHOWN=y
CONFIG_SU=y
CONFIG_SHA256SUM=y
CONFIG_CUT=y
CONFIG_TR=y
CONFIG_MV=y
CONFIG_CP=y
CONFIG_IP=y
CONFIG_FEATURE_IP_ADDRESS=y
CONFIG_FEATURE_IP_LINK=y
CONFIG_UDHCPD=y
